  "summary": "0-bg grid (size varies). TOP LIBRARY rows hold 2-4 PANELS separated by FULL-LIBRARY-HEIGHT COLOR-9 divider columns; each panel has one COLOR-9 ANCHOR plus a RANDOM STENCIL of 1-5 cells in ONE non-9 color at random offsets from the anchor. A fully-blank row separates the library from the BODY below, which holds scattered cells in the library colors. Rule: detect the library (above the first blank row), split it into panels by the 9-columns, read each panel's (color, stencil-offsets-from-anchor); for each body cell of color C, STAMP C's stencil at that cell onto a blank output (in-bounds offsets only). Net: each body cell expands into its library-stencil shape.",
